REQUIREMENTS

IsaLibs works with Isabelle2026 (October 2026), https://isabelle.in.tum.de/

The IsaLibs session (IsaLibs/ROOT) is based on HOL and also uses the theory
THF_Arith from the HOL-TPTP session of the Isabelle distribution. The theory
IsaLibs is declared "global", so user theories can simply say "imports IsaLibs".

Build the IsaLibs heap image once with:

isabelle build -d path_to_IsaLibs_root_file -b IsaLibs

DOCUMENTATION

doc/IsaLibs_comandos.pdf (Spanish) explains every Isar command, proof method,
attribute and configuration option of IsaLibs, and the theory behind them.
Rebuild it with "cd doc && latexmk -pdf IsaLibs_comandos.tex" (or "make -C doc").

PAPERS

papers/divergent-completion-iterated-functions contains an article (for the
Journal of Symbolic Computation) on the tower critic of "complete", together with
the Isabelle theories of its experiments.

papers/abc-theory-repair contains an extension of IsaScheme with the faults and
repair operations of the ABC system of Bundy and colleagues, in its own session
ABC_Repair, together with the examples of the ABC chapter, a pilot on recursive
functions and an article that describes them. Build it with

isabelle build -d IsaLibs -d papers/abc-theory-repair ABC_Repair

WINDOWS INSTALLATION

1) Create a theory file. The name of the theory is not important but you must import IsaLibs.

theory MyTheory
imports IsaLibs
begin

end

2) Create a new settings file or edit your existing one to include the following path. Note that IsaLibs comes with a working timeout tool.

TIMEAOUT_PATH=path_to_timeout

e.g.

TIMEAOUT_PATH=/cygdrive/c/Users/Omar/Programs/IsaLibs

3) Download the AProVE termination prover (command line version) from the link and place it on the same directory of your theory file (see step 1).

http://aprove.informatik.rwth-aachen.de/

3.1) Install dependencies:
     CeTa: http://cl-informatik.uibk.ac.at/software/ceta/#downloads

4) Run the following command to build the heap image and work with your theory

isabelle jedit -d path_to_IsaLibs_root_file -l IsaLibs your_theory.thy

LINUX/MAC OS X INSTALLATION

1) Create a theory file. The name of the theory is not important but you must import IsaLibs.

theory MyTheory
imports IsaLibs
begin

end

2) Download the AProVE termination prover (aprove.jar, it needs Java) from the link and place it on any directory such as 'path_to_AProVE_jar_file'.

https://github.com/aprove-developers/aprove-releases/releases

AProVE looks for the SAT solver "minisat2" in the PATH. Isabelle ships one, so it is enough to link it, e.g.

mkdir -p path_to_AProVE_jar_file/bin
ln -s $ISABELLE_HOME/contrib/minisat-*/x86_64-linux/minisat path_to_AProVE_jar_file/bin/minisat2

3) Create a new settings file (e.g. $ISABELLE_HOME_USER/etc/settings, that is ~/.isabelle/Isabelle2026/etc/settings) or edit your existing one to include the following paths. Note that IsaLibs comes with a working timeout tool (the script "timeout" in this directory).

APROVE_PATH=path_to_AProVE_jar_file
TIMEAOUT_PATH=path_to_timeout
APROVE_SERVER=localhost
APROVE_SERVER_PORT=5250
PATH="path_to_AProVE_jar_file/bin:$PATH"

IsaLibs.thy sets use_aprove_srv = true, so AProVE is called through a server (and nc). Start the server before running IsaLibs:

cd path_to_AProVE_jar_file && PATH="path_to_AProVE_jar_file/bin:$PATH" java -ea -jar aprove.jar -u srv

Alternatively, declare [[use_aprove_srv = false]] to run aprove.jar directly for each termination check (slower).

The server can get stuck, typically after interrupting a diverging "complete". It then keeps listening on port 5250 but answers TIMEOUT to everything. To check it, send it a trivial TRS and make sure that the first line of the answer is YES:

printf '(VAR x)\n(RULES f(s(x)) -> f(x))\n' > /tmp/prueba.trs
printf '2\n/tmp/prueba.trs\n5\n' | nc localhost 5250 | head -1

If it does not answer YES, restart the server:

pkill -f 'aprove.jar -u srv'
cd path_to_AProVE_jar_file && PATH="path_to_AProVE_jar_file/bin:$PATH" java -ea -jar aprove.jar -u srv

(or, in the background: ... nohup java -ea -jar aprove.jar -u srv > server.out 2>&1 &)

Then restart Isabelle/jEdit as well, because termination results, including the false ones given by the stuck server, are memoized for the lifetime of the Isabelle process.

4) Run the following command to build the heap image and work with your theory

isabelle jedit -d path_to_IsaLibs_root_file -l IsaLibs your_theory.thy


— Build IsaLibs —

isabelle build -d /Users/omarmrivas/Programs/IsaLibs/IsaLibs -b IsaLibs


